TI Trust Technologies OV CA — intermediate of www.italgiure.giustizia.it

The Italgiure server sends the wrong intermediates (the DV CA and an unrelated
GeoTrust CA) instead of the one that signed its certificate, so a client that
only trusts the public roots cannot build the chain. This is that missing
intermediate, as published at the certificate's own AIA address
(http://tiTrust.crt.sectigo.com/TITrustTechnologiesOVCA.crt). It is signed by
USERTrust RSA Certification Authority, a root in certifi, so the chain still
ends at a public root: this file adds no trust of its own.

subject:  C=IT, ST=Roma, L=Pomezia, O=TI Trust Technologies S.R.L., CN=TI Trust Technologies OV CA
issuer:   C=US, ST=New Jersey, L=Jersey City, O=The USERTRUST Network, CN=USERTrust RSA Certification Authority
